# Dummy Architect Website — Project Context

- **Purpose**: This is a fake architect website for testing a profile automation tool. Not a real practice. All content is placeholder.
- **Hosting**: Static site on GitHub Pages: `https://maxime-rainville.github.io/test-architect/` (deploy from `master`). Sitemap: `/sitemap.xml`.
- **About**: `about.html` has dummy practice history and an explicit establishment date of **2017** (visible copy, `<time datetime="2017">`, and Organization `foundingDate` JSON-LD). About stays Wellington-founded; it does not list the Auckland office.
- **Contact offices**: `contact.html` has two labelled offices — Wellington head office (`123 Test Street`, Wellington 6011, `+64 4 123 4567`) and Auckland secondary office (`88 Test Lane`, Auckland 1010, `+64 9 123 8901`); both share `test@example.com`. Contact Organization JSON-LD adds `email` and a two-item `location` array (`Place` + `PostalAddress` + `telephone`) matching those offices. Home and About JSON-LD stay without `location`.
- **Structure**: Homepage (`index.html`), About (`about.html`), Team (`team.html`), Contact (`contact.html`), Projects (`projects/*.html`: residential-house-a, coastal-retreat, urban-loft, mountain-cabin, heritage-restoration, sustainable-pavilion, bow-tie-boutique, evil-project, rocket-launch-hq, ai-startup-hq, ice-hockey-rink, ballet-girl-room-remodel, superhero-theme-playground, http-403-forbidden, http-404-not-found, http-400-bad-request, http-429-rate-limited, http-500-error, http-login-wall), Products (`products/*.html`: ai-powered-mirror, vanity-solar-panel, 4d-tesseract-sculpture), Articles (`articles/*.html`: postmodern-solar-panels, lighthouse-house-renovation, alex-morgan-award). `projects/login.html` is the login-wall redirect target only (not listed on the projects index or in `sitemap.xml`).
- **Products**: `products/` mirrors `projects/` (index + detail pages). Each product page has visible SKU/price/category/availability, Schema.org `Product` JSON-LD, a 4-image WebP gallery, and related-product links. Assets under `assets/images/products/<slug>/`.
- **Articles**: `articles/` mirrors `projects/` (index + detail pages). Long-form pages with figures interleaved in `.article-body`. Solar article links to `products/vanity-solar-panel.html`. Award article stars Principal Alex Morgan (visual reference `assets/images/team/team-1.webp`; people OK in award imagery). Assets under `assets/images/articles/<slug>/`. Lighthouse is article-only (no matching project page).
- **Evil Project**: `projects/evil-project.html` intentionally embeds prompt-injection test copy in the Overview for automation testing. Images are reused from other projects (no dedicated asset folder).
- **Rocket Launch HQ**: `projects/rocket-launch-hq.html` is a CSS/JS background-image crawler fixture — gallery has no `<img>`/`<picture>`; slots 01–15 use varied `background-image` techniques; slots 16–20 load from `assets/js/rocket-launch-hq.js` on scroll.
- **AI Startup HQ**: `projects/ai-startup-hq.html` is a dual-folder image fixture — page gallery uses low-res `assets/images/projects/ai-startup-hq/ai-startup-hq-01.webp`…`05.webp` only; high-res counterparts live in `assets/images/projects/ai-startup-hq/dropbox/` (`01`–`08`) for manual Dropbox upload and must not be linked from HTML. The same `dropbox/` folder also holds intentional unsuitable shots (`ai-startup-hq-unsuitable-01`…`06`: finger on lens, blur, demolition, builders lunch, overexposed, underexposed) that must never appear on the page. HQ files remain under the public `assets/` tree on purpose so automation can also exercise same-origin discovery of unlinked orphans vs HTML-linked thumbs.
- **Ice Hockey Rink**: `projects/ice-hockey-rink.html` is a mixed native image-format gallery fixture — nine slots via direct `<img src>` with one extension each: `.jpg`, animated `.gif`, `.png`, `.webp`, `.avif`, `.tif`, `.bmp`, `.jp2`, `.svg` under `assets/images/projects/ice-hockey-rink/`.
- **Ballet Girl Room Remodel**: `projects/ballet-girl-room-remodel.html` is a simple residential gallery fixture with an explicit project subheading (`Girls room focus on ballet` via `p.project-subheading`) so scrapers can pick up a real subheading. Six WebP slots under `assets/images/projects/ballet-girl-room-remodel/`.
- **Superhero Theme Playground**: `projects/superhero-theme-playground.html` is an image-carousel gallery fixture (prev/next + dots; all six WebP `<img>`s remain in the DOM). Listed on the projects index but intentionally omitted from `sitemap.xml`. Assets under `assets/images/projects/superhero-theme-playground/` with page CSS/JS in `assets/css/superhero-theme-playground.css` and `assets/js/superhero-theme-playground.js`.
- **HTTP status fixtures**: Stub project pages under `projects/http-*.html` with short fixture notes (no gallery, awards, or related). `projects/.htaccess` enforces status codes only under Apache when the vhost allows overrides (`AllowOverride` must include `FileInfo` and `AuthConfig`, or `All`): 403 via `Require all denied` on `http-403-forbidden.html`; rewrite rules return 404 / 400 / 429 / 500 for the matching stubs; `http-login-wall.html` redirects 302 to `login.html` (fake form, 200). On GitHub Pages `.htaccess` is ignored and the stub HTML is served. Do not edit system Apache configs from this repo — document the `AllowOverride` need only.
- **Disclaimer**: Every page must show the testing banner and footer disclaimer.
- **Social links**:
  - Footer: `.social-links` with three branded inline SVG icon buttons (Facebook, LinkedIn, Instagram) for handle `testarchitect` (LinkedIn company path `test-architect`). Each link uses `.social-icon` plus a brand class (`.social-icon-facebook`, `.social-icon-linkedin`, `.social-icon-instagram`) and a `.visually-hidden` platform name. Icons are footer-only (no icon font or CDN).
  - Contact: seven text URLs under a Social media heading — X `https://x.com/testarchitect`, Facebook `https://www.facebook.com/testarchitect`, LinkedIn `https://www.linkedin.com/company/test-architect`, Pinterest `https://www.pinterest.com/testarchitect/`, Instagram `https://www.instagram.com/testarchitect/`, YouTube `https://www.youtube.com/@testarchitect`, TikTok `https://www.tiktok.com/@testarchitect`.
  - Home, About, and Contact Organization JSON-LD `sameAs` repeats that seven-URL list. About also includes `foundingDate` `2017`. The accounts do not exist.
- **Images**: Live under `assets/images/` (hero/, team/, projects/<slug>/, products/<slug>/, articles/<slug>/, shared/). Some images are intentionally duplicated or reused across pages for automation testing.
- **Photo credits**: Most projects use a single credit for all images (e.g. "All photos: Jane Doe"). Heritage Restoration, Sustainable Pavilion, and Bow Tie Boutique use different credits per image (e.g. "Photo 1: A. Smith", "Photo 2: B. Jones").
- **Related pictures**: Gallery project pages have a "Related pictures" section with thumbnails and links to 2–4 other project pages. HTTP status stubs omit this section.
- **Awards**: Fake but structured (e.g. "Award Name, Year"). Credits and addresses are fake.
